# Netlify header rules for the DataAgent marketing site.
#
# The same header set is declared in netlify.toml and vercel.json. Keep the
# three in sync - tests/test_launch_site_launch_readiness.py asserts that the
# three sets are IDENTICAL, so that a host change cannot silently drop one.
#
# The site is served entirely from this repository: no CDN, no tracker, no
# analytics, no webfont from a third party. Every asset is same-origin, so
# the policy below can be this strict.
#
# On the Content-Security-Policy:
#   - 'unsafe-inline' is still needed for script-src and style-src: the pages
#     carry inline <script> blocks (the Three.js import map, a few small
#     bootstraps) and inline style attributes. The goal is to remove them
#     and to drop 'unsafe-inline' from this policy - until then it stays,
#     because a policy without it breaks the site.
#   - https://checkout.razorpay.com is the ONE documented exception: the
#     pricing page injects Razorpay's hosted checkout script when a buyer
#     clicks Buy on a deployment that has a billing server configured. It
#     is a user-initiated payment hand-off, not a page-view beacon, and it
#     is the only third-party script the site is allowed to load. Remove
#     it if the deployment uses the same-origin Payment Link fallback.
#   - connect-src allows the billing API on pay.data-agent.me. It is a
#     same-site subdomain of this storefront, so the account cookie is sent
#     and the API answers with explicit CORS credentials for this origin.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://checkout.razorpay.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://pay.data-agent.me; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
# `same-origin-allow-popups`, NOT `same-origin`: the SPA opens the Google
# OAuth popup with window.open() and the callback posts back through
# window.opener. `same-origin` severs the opener and forces sign-in onto a
# weaker polling fallback. See web/js/auth.js::_waitForGoogleResult.
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
